.github.com/repos/psf/black/labels/F:%20trailing%20comma","name":"F: trailing comma","color":"BFD4F2","default":false,"description":"Full of magic"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2022-08-02T20:26:14Z","updated_at":"2022-08-05T03:20:56Z","closed_at":"2022-08-05T03:20:55Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nTrailing commas inside indexing square brackets are not removed when running Black with `-C`. This also affects generic types with multiple parameters.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\nFor example, take this code:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nx = [0, 1,]\r\nx = z[0, 1,]\r\n```\r\n\r\nand run with `-C`. We get\r\n\r\n```python\r\nx = [0, 1]\r\nx = z[0, 1,]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nThe final trailing comma should disappear.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nx = z[0, 1]\r\n```\r\n**Environment**\r\n\r\n<!-- Please complete the following information: -->\r\n\r\n- Black's version: 22.6.0. Also tested on main on the playground, and with/without `--preview`.\r\n- OS and Python version: Linux/Python 3.10.5","closed_by":{"login":"ichard26","id":63936253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTM2MjUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63936253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26","html_url":"https://github.com/ichard26","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ichard26/o